Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.00,0:00:31.02,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,Back in Graycastle,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.02,0:00:35.26,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,Fourth Prince Roland Wimbledon \Nwas already notorious.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.26,0:00:37.76,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,A life of debauchery, utter incompetence,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.76,0:00:41.29,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,not a shred of noble grace... \Nthe list goes on.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.29,0:00:45.95,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,Compared to his four siblings, \Nhe was worlds apart.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.95,0:00:51.00,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,Ah, why was I sent to assist \Nhim in the Royal Decree?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.00,0:00:53.99,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,If His Majesty hadn't promised \Nto appoint me as the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.99,0:00:56.56,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,official Finance Minister once \Nthe Royal Decree concluded,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.56,0:00:59.44,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,I wouldn't have come to \Nthis godforsaken place.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.44,0:01:02.70,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,And yet, things began to change.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.70,0:01:05.85,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,When exactly did it start?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.37,0:01:11.22,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,Probably around the time \Nhe saved that witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.22,0:01:15.70,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,His Highness Roland displayed a \Nsharp mind and grand strategic vision.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.70,0:01:17.99,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,He skillfully avoided his own predicament,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.99,0:01:20.71,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,and struck at the very \Nessence of theocracy.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.71,0:01:25.60,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,By using witches, he set his sights \Ndirectly on the Church of Hermes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.60,0:01:29.28,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,At first, I thought it was \Njust baseless rhetoric.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.28,0:01:32.44,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,But then, His Highness spent all night \Nstudying financial reports,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.44,0:01:34.13,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,formulating trade strategies,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.13,0:01:37.60,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,and even proposed something \Ncalled the "Silk Road."
Dialogue: 0,0:01:37.60,0:01:40.84,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,Heaven knows where he learned those words.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.84,0:01:43.23,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,Still, to possess such a long-term vision,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.23,0:01:47.56,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,while keeping his focus squarely on the \Nimmediate development of Border Town,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.56,0:01:50.40,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,this is no baseless fantasy.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.40,0:01:53.85,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,But if we cannot survive \Nthe Months of Demons,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.85,0:01:56.82,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,everything will be for nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.82,0:02:01.73,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,I hear from Carter that His Highness \Nnow plans to build a city wall.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.73,0:02:04.87,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,Winter is just over three months away.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.87,0:02:08.84,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,Even if it's only around 2000 feet long, \Nit should be theoretically impossible.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.84,0:02:12.23,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,But His Highness has already \Nsurprised me so many times.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.23,0:02:13.57,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,There's still three months left.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.57,0:02:17.73,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,If it really can't be done, \Nthere's still time to run away.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.73,0:02:22.82,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,How will His Highness build a \Ncity wall in just three months?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:22.82,0:02:26.50,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,From here on, things are only \Ngetting more interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.39,0:04:40.50,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Be careful. Move it over there.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.33,0:04:51.40,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Go to the North Mountain mine and \Nbring back a cartload of limestone.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.40,0:04:53.85,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Also get a cartload of clay, \Nsomething like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.75,0:04:58.03,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Then have someone crush them into \Nsmall pieces, mix them thoroughly,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.03,0:05:00.64,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and spread the mixture evenly \Nin the pit in the firing room.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.45,0:05:10.02,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Leave the rest to Miss Anna.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.25,0:05:44.08,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Carter, get someone to \Ncrush this clinker.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.08,0:05:46.79,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Mix it with gypsum at a 10:1 \Nratio and grind it into powder.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.79,0:05:49.27,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Your Highness, what is this for?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.56,0:05:52.27,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,A new formula from the alchemy workshop.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.59,0:05:56.92,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Your Highness, everything is \Nprepared as you instructed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.72,0:05:59.34,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,What exactly are you making?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.20,0:06:09.22,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Miss Anna, this time, \Nlet me show you a bit of magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.53,0:06:11.72,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Your Highness, you can use magic too?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.64,0:06:16.56,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Yes. A kind of magic called science.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.56,0:06:17.64,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Science?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.64,0:06:21.92,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Carter, mix this powder with water \Nand pour it onto those stones over there.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.92,0:06:25.46,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Pour it into the gaps, so that it's \Nevenly spread between the stones.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.46,0:06:28.52,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,By tomorrow, they will \Nbecome a solid wall.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.52,0:06:31.12,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Huh? You must be joking!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.12,0:06:32.97,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Miss Anna, do you believe me?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.67,0:06:36.97,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Whatever you say, I believe you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.20,0:06:39.47,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Then do as I say.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.47,0:06:41.10,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Let's wait and see.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.92,0:06:44.40,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Y-Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.12,0:06:56.26,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Go on, Carter.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.84,0:06:58.30,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Test its strength.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.49,0:07:17.64,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,T-This is truly incredible, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.19,0:07:21.18,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,With this, we can build our \Ncity wall as fast as we want.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.18,0:07:24.14,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,A border wall in five years \Nwould be well within reach.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.14,0:07:26.16,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,We could even use it to \Nreinforce this castle,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.16,0:07:29.34,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,making it the strongest, \Nsafest castle in Graycastle.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.34,0:07:30.58,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Not just the castle.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.58,0:07:32.64,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,We'll use it to build much more.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.99,0:07:34.44,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Much more?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.39,0:07:42.95,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,{\i1}Could I have ten thousand mansions,{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.95,0:07:46.39,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,{\i1}sheltering all the poor scholars \Nand making them rejoice.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.28,0:07:49.11,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Your Highness, what did you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.08,0:07:53.89,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,We'll use it to build a \Nbetter home for everyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.62,0:07:57.12,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Everyone can live in a sturdy house,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.12,0:07:59.89,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,one that neither storms \Nnor blizzards can destroy.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.84,0:08:04.51,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Miss Anna, starting today,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.51,0:08:06.26,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,please fire a batch every day.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.82,0:08:08.39,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.26,0:08:12.10,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Carter, you're in charge \Nof wall construction.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.10,0:08:14.11,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Make sure it's built within three months.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.11,0:08:15.27,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.27,0:08:16.33,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Leave it to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.29,0:08:24.52,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Oh, by the way, Your Highness,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.52,0:08:27.39,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,what is this miraculous \Nalchemical powder called?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.44,0:08:32.46,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Cement.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.39,0:08:40.72,Italics,Roland,0,0,0,,What... What is this?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.40,0:08:49.93,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.93,0:08:51.11,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,So many days have passed.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.11,0:08:53.05,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Why is construction moving so slowly?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.05,0:08:54.89,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,And it's crooked and uneven.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.89,0:08:56.45,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You can't even stand on it properly.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.45,0:08:58.00,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Forget holding off demonic beasts,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.00,0:08:59.14,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,it'd collapse in the first rain.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.14,0:09:00.39,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Apologies, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.39,0:09:01.68,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,It is my responsibility.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.12,0:09:05.36,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Your Highness, if I may speak frankly,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.36,0:09:08.09,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Carter has no prior \Nexperience in such matters.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.09,0:09:10.02,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,For a wall over 2000 feet long,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.02,0:09:13.84,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,without an experienced architect \Nto oversee the work,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.84,0:09:18.86,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,even with this miraculous \Nalchemical agent called "cement,"
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.86,0:09:21.68,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,it would be difficult to meet \NYour Highness's expectations.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.09,0:09:25.70,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,We need a true master stonemason.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.70,0:09:26.97,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,A master stonemason...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.72,0:09:31.36,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Go and recruit one immediately, \Nno matter the cost.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.36,0:09:34.42,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,But Your Highness, \Nit's not a matter of money.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.42,0:09:38.56,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,There's no one with this kind \Nof expertise in Border Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.56,0:09:41.41,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Then look for one in \NLongsong Stronghold or Willow Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.41,0:09:44.30,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Even if you have to go back \Nto Graycastle, find someone.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.68,0:10:26.99,Flashback,Nana,0,0,0,,Professor Karl!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.70,0:10:31.85,Flashback,Nana,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.84,0:10:33.85,Flashback,Nana,0,0,0,,I've become...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.42,0:10:37.85,Flashback,Nana,0,0,0,,I've become a witch too.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.86,0:10:43.68,Main,Villager,0,0,0,,Mr. van Bate, could you \Nplease come over here?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.57,0:10:49.48,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,What's happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.48,0:10:51.50,Main,Villager,0,0,0,,Please take a look at this notice for us.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.50,0:10:53.47,Main,Villager,0,0,0,,They say the prince posted it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.47,0:10:55.35,Main,Villager,0,0,0,,What does it say?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.35,0:10:57.13,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,By decree of Roland Wimbledon,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.13,0:10:59.10,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Fourth Prince of\Nthe Kingdom of Graycastle:
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.10,0:11:01.56,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Urgent recruitment for \Nthe following positions:
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.56,0:11:06.39,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Stonebreakers: male, \Nages 20 - 40, physically strong.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.39,0:11:08.48,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Daily wage: 25 bronze royals.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.48,0:11:12.62,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Masons: Any gender, \Nages 18+, with masonry experience.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.62,0:11:14.78,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Daily wage: 45 bronze royals.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.78,0:11:17.90,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Laborers: male, ages 18+.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.90,0:11:19.87,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Daily wage: 12 bronze royals.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.87,0:11:22.99,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Master stonemasons: Any gender, any age.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.99,0:11:24.94,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Must have experience in \Nmunicipal construction,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.94,0:11:27.52,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,fortress building, \Nor large-scale engineering projects.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.52,0:11:29.40,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Monthly wage: 1 gold royal.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.40,0:11:31.43,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Those with exceptional \Nexperience and performance
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.43,0:11:32.78,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,may be granted official positions.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.78,0:11:36.35,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Fourth Prince of the \NKingdom of Graycastle, Roland Wimbledon.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.35,0:11:37.32,Main,Villager,0,0,0,,Did I hear that right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.32,0:11:39.12,Main,Villager,0,0,0,,You could even become an official,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.12,0:11:41.35,Main,Villager,0,0,0,,maybe see His Highness \Nthe Prince every day!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.33,0:11:44.43,Main,Villager,0,0,0,,Mr. van Bate, Mr. van Bate!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.28,0:11:49.83,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,A master stonemason came \Nto apply so quickly?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.83,0:11:51.85,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Didn't you say finding one would be hard?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.85,0:11:53.44,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,I'm surprised too.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.44,0:11:55.82,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,The man is clearly a local teacher,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.82,0:11:59.53,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,yet he claims to have experience \Nin large-scale construction projects.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.53,0:12:01.73,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Your Highness, would you like to see him?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.88,0:12:05.05,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Of course. Bring him in.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.68,0:12:07.85,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,So you're here to apply \Nas master stonemason?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.85,0:12:09.28,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.28,0:12:11.90,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,My name is Karl van Bate.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.90,0:12:14.85,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I heard you used to teach in town.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.85,0:12:17.98,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I just taught the children to recognize \Ntheir names, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.98,0:12:19.89,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Then what qualifies you for this position?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.89,0:12:24.69,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I... have participated in the maintenance \Nof embankments within Graycastle,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.69,0:12:26.35,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,the design and construction of the palace,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.35,0:12:29.35,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,and the renovation of \Nvarious public facilities.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.58,0:12:34.43,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You mean you've been involved in many \Nmajor construction projects in Graycastle?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.15,0:12:37.43,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.43,0:12:39.97,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,All large-scale construction in Graycastle
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.97,0:12:42.26,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,is handled by the Mason Guild.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.26,0:12:45.18,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Are you a member of the \NGraycastle Mason Guild?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.41,0:12:48.20,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.01,0:12:51.02,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The Mason Guild's members \Nare naturally elites.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.02,0:12:54.11,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,But as I recall, during construction of \Nthe Graycastle Theater a few years ago,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.11,0:12:55.97,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,a collapse occurred.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.97,0:12:57.93,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The entire Mason Guild was convicted
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.93,0:12:59.22,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and executed.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.46,0:13:04.15,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,That is indeed how the \Nstory spread outside.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.15,0:13:06.69,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Oh? Then what really happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.22,0:13:09.15,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,The administrator at the time,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.15,0:13:11.26,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,for a kickback of several \Nhundred gold royals,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.26,0:13:13.16,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,ordered us to switch the stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.16,0:13:15.24,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,which led to the accident.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.24,0:13:17.76,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,We warned the administrator \Nmany times that
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.76,0:13:21.72,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,using that grade of stone would \Ncompromise structural integrity.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.72,0:13:23.65,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,But no one listened.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.65,0:13:25.28,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,After the accident,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.28,0:13:28.16,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,we explained everything \Nto the investigators.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.16,0:13:31.67,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,But the official who \Nordered the substitution
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.67,0:13:33.51,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,claimed that it was to save costs.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.08,0:13:37.97,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,In the end, he was deemed to have \Ngood intentions and was acquitted.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:37.97,0:13:41.75,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,The entire Mason Guild \Nwas sentenced to death.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.35,0:13:45.35,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I heard rumors beforehand \Nand fled overnight.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.35,0:13:48.22,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I came to Border Town \Nand have hidden my identity ever since.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.83,0:13:50.72,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,If you've been hiding your identity,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.72,0:13:53.22,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,why are you revealing yourself \Nand applying for the job now?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.04,0:13:57.60,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Because...  I have a reason \NI can no longer stay silent.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.60,0:13:58.62,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,What reason?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.48,0:14:00.11,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.36,0:14:02.85,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:02.85,0:14:05.22,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I cannot yet reveal my reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.61,0:14:06.51,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Your Highness,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.91,0:14:10.14,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I know you have doubts about me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.46,0:14:13.86,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,After all, I defied the investigation \Nand fled, a capital offense.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.86,0:14:15.69,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,But I really had no choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.69,0:14:18.03,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,If I hadn't fled, \NI wouldn't be alive today.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.60,0:14:20.28,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I've been a stonemason my whole life.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.28,0:14:22.06,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I can definitely meet your requirements.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.06,0:14:25.17,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Please give me a chance \Nto atone for my sins.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.98,0:14:30.68,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Barov, what do you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.68,0:14:35.27,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Your Highness, I believe this \Nman is mostly telling the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.27,0:14:39.22,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,By law, he is now a fugitive \Nguilty of a crime.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.22,0:14:42.96,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,However, considering your \Ncurrent needs, Your Highness,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.62,0:14:47.13,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,I think it would be wise \Nto make an exception.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.78,0:14:54.18,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Mr. van Bate, I pardon your crimes \Nand appoint you as Master Stonemason.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.18,0:14:57.32,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,From now on, you're a member \Nof the administrative office.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:57.32,0:15:00.31,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Show me what a master \Nfrom the Mason Guild can do.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.83,0:15:05.74,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I want to build a city wall here,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.74,0:15:07.87,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,from the Dragonspine Mountain \Nto the Redwater River,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.87,0:15:09.97,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,roughly 2000 feet in length.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.55,0:15:12.30,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Fifteen feet high, six feet wide,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.30,0:15:14.45,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,wide enough for four men to walk abreast.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.45,0:15:16.56,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Well? How would you go about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.35,0:15:20.09,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,First, to stabilize the upper structure,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.09,0:15:22.01,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,we'll need to dig a trench one man deep.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.01,0:15:26.71,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,And if the top is six feet wide \Nand the wall is 15 feet high,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.71,0:15:29.22,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,then the base must be at \Nleast twice that width.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.84,0:15:31.74,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,If Your Highness provides me with 150 men,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.74,0:15:33.89,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I can complete the trench in three months.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.40,0:15:37.10,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,The upper wall must be \Nbuilt with solid stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.10,0:15:39.62,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Cutting and polishing the \Nstone will take a lot of time.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.62,0:15:42.21,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,The whole project will probably \Ntake three years to complete.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.47,0:15:48.74,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,A ditch won't stop the demonic beasts.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.74,0:15:50.16,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Stop the demonic beasts...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.16,0:15:51.98,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,You... You mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.47,0:15:56.49,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Yes. I need to build a wall \Ncapable of holding back demonic beasts.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.49,0:15:59.78,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Therefore, it must be completed before \Nthe Months of Demons arrive this year.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.78,0:16:00.60,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Can it be done?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.61,0:16:04.60,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Well, if that's the case...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.61,0:16:07.99,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Then the wall doesn't need \Nto be built that high.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.60,0:16:09.71,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Like this...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.58,0:16:12.88,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,If the height is reduced to 12 feet,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.88,0:16:15.28,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,and the width reduced by a third,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.28,0:16:18.30,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,then the base width shrinks to 6 feet.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.30,0:16:20.83,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,We can dig the trench and \Nbuild the wall simultaneously.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.83,0:16:24.02,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,If we increase the workforce to 200,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.02,0:16:28.68,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,the foundation could be dug \Nin about a month and a half.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.68,0:16:30.09,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.09,0:16:31.02,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,But what?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.01,0:16:35.16,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Building the wall requires \Na lot of cut stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.16,0:16:36.88,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,In such a short time,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.88,0:16:39.10,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,there's no way we can \Nprocess enough stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.10,0:16:41.44,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Even if we bought it from nearby towns,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.44,0:16:43.56,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,factoring in transport time,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.56,0:16:45.54,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I'm afraid it's still...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:45.54,0:16:47.54,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,So if we had enough stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.54,0:16:49.82,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,you could build the wall \Nwithin three months?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.82,0:16:51.68,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I believe so, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.68,0:16:52.38,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.38,0:16:53.84,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Then you don't need to worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.37,0:16:56.56,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Come with me. \NI'll show you something.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.52,0:16:59.16,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Oh, okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.29,0:17:06.45,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,This is amazing.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.45,0:17:07.74,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,It's incredible!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.77,0:17:11.88,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,They... They've bonded so solidly.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.64,0:17:16.62,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,With this, it's like having stone \Nblocks in any shape we need,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.62,0:17:18.78,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,without cutting or polishing.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.17,0:17:25.56,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,If we can eliminate the \Ntime-consuming step of processing stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.56,0:17:27.39,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,the speed of any construction project
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.39,0:17:28.90,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,will reach an entirely new level.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:28.90,0:17:31.89,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Well? With this, can you \Nfinish in three months?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.89,0:17:34.54,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Yes. This substance is magnificent.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.54,0:17:37.04,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Your Highness, what did \Nyou say it was called?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.04,0:17:37.80,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Cement.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.80,0:17:39.97,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Cement. I'll remember that.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.97,0:17:44.51,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I can't believe the alchemy workshop \Ndeveloped something this amazing.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.51,0:17:48.19,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I'll write you some detailed \Ninstructions on how to use cement.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.19,0:17:51.14,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,If you need anything else, \Nspeak with my assistant minister, Barov.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.99,0:17:53.25,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.93,0:17:58.48,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Your Highness, actually, \Nthere's one more thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.48,0:17:59.99,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Oh? What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.99,0:18:01.01,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,It's...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.94,0:18:05.96,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Anna!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.57,0:18:10.03,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Professor Karl!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.08,0:18:18.84,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,So, he's the aforementioned Professor Karl.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.84,0:18:22.96,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Yes, many of the town's children \Ngo to his house for lessons.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.96,0:18:24.62,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,He's really kind to us.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.43,0:18:29.44,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I only told them stories \Nand taught them a few words.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.44,0:18:32.53,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Anna, I thought you were dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.53,0:18:35.61,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I've been having nightmares \Nthese past few days.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.61,0:18:38.09,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,It's such a relief you're alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.41,0:18:40.06,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.56,0:18:44.06,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Your Highness, thank you for your mercy.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.40,0:18:46.11,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Don't be like that. Please get up.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.10,0:18:48.10,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Your Highness...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.10,0:18:51.00,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Mr. van Bate, to me,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:51.00,0:18:53.46,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,witches aren't the \Nembodiment of the Devil.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.46,0:18:56.44,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I certainly won't hunt them \Ndown as the Church commands.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.44,0:18:58.26,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Miss Anna is innocent.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.26,0:18:59.79,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Of course I'd never harm her.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.79,0:19:02.86,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Your Highness, \Nthere's something I must tell you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.19,0:19:08.06,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Oh, what is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.06,0:19:10.86,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Do you remember I mentioned earlier
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.86,0:19:13.55,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,that I had my own reason \Nfor coming to apply?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.55,0:19:15.33,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I didn't dare tell you then,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.33,0:19:19.04,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,but now, I'm certain I can.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.04,0:19:23.06,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,In this Border Town, \Nthere is another witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.25,0:19:37.68,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,How can this be?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.27,0:19:42.68,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Even Nana... has become a witch too?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.68,0:19:45.65,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Who would've thought that \Nin this tiny Border Town,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.65,0:19:47.13,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,there would be two witches?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.13,0:19:48.64,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,If this were anywhere else,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.64,0:19:52.02,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,there would be another bloody witch hunt.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.02,0:19:57.28,Italics,Barov,0,0,0,,But how will His Highness react here?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.70,0:20:05.68,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,This is what I wish to ask \Nof you, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.68,0:20:08.42,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Your Highness is merciful and \Nunafraid of the rumors of the Devil.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.42,0:20:12.18,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,It's Anna's good fortune \Nto be able to join your harem.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.76,0:20:16.54,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Although Nana is still \Nyoung and cannot serve you,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.54,0:20:18.24,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,she is truly innocent.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.24,0:20:20.31,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I beg you, Your Highness,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.31,0:20:21.68,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,please save her too.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.17,0:20:24.61,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It's not what you think.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.61,0:20:27.36,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I saved Anna because I need her help.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:27.36,0:20:29.84,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I-I believe that once Nana grows up,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.84,0:20:31.68,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,she'll definitely be able to help you too.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.67,0:20:36.54,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You truly misunderstand.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.54,0:20:41.18,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Miss Anna's job is to make \Nthe cement I just showed you.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.18,0:20:42.19,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.83,0:20:46.18,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,That miraculous substance \Nwas actually made by Anna?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:46.86,0:20:48.41,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,As for this Nana you mentioned,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.41,0:20:49.76,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I'd like to meet her.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.76,0:20:51.70,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I can guarantee her safety.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.70,0:20:53.03,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Could you bring her to me?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.03,0:20:55.03,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Ah! Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.03,0:20:56.18,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.18,0:20:57.86,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Forgive me, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.86,0:21:00.70,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I... I am truly grateful to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.14,0:21:05.34,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Let's go. We'll discuss \Ndetails back in my chambers.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.06,0:21:07.05,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.01,0:21:10.73,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Miss Anna, I'll leave matters here to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.73,0:21:12.06,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.78,0:21:17.66,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Your Highness. Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.66,0:21:18.60,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,What is it, Barov?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.60,0:21:22.35,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Your Highness, I understand \Nyour eagerness to meet this witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.35,0:21:25.61,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,However, there might be a complication.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.61,0:21:27.51,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Oh? What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.51,0:21:31.89,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,You see, this girl's name \Nis Nana Pine, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.89,0:21:34.82,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,The surname Pine doesn't \Nbelong to commoners.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.82,0:21:38.62,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,It belongs to a minor \Nnoble in town, Baron Pine.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:39.55,0:21:40.96,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Is that so?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.96,0:21:42.48,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.48,0:21:45.72,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Nana is indeed the daughter \Nof Baron Tigui Pine.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.97,0:21:49.93,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,If the nobles find out, \Nit could be troublesome.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.99,0:21:54.32,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Mr. van Bate, bring Nana \Nhere tomorrow morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.32,0:21:55.84,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Come at the usual lesson time.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.84,0:21:56.83,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Don't draw attention.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.83,0:21:58.05,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.62,0:22:01.44,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Barov, once Nana arrives tomorrow,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.44,0:22:02.91,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,take her directly to the kitchen.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.91,0:22:04.67,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Clear the area beforehand.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.67,0:22:06.16,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I'll meet her in the kitchen.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.69,0:22:09.39,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Very wise, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.83,0:22:41.06,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.58,0:22:42.85,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Miss Pine is here.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.25,0:22:54.45,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,It's all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.86,0:22:57.81,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Go on, Nana.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:58.32,0:22:59.74,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Greet His Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.85,0:23:03.38,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,H-Hello.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:03.38,0:23:07.02,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,I-I'm Nana Pine, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:07.95,0:23:09.87,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Hello, Miss Pine.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.04,0:23:13.02,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Welcome. Please have a seat.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:20.71,0:23:22.96,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Go on, it's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:22.96,0:23:24.92,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,His Highness is asking you to sit.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.92,0:23:26.54,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Go ahead, it's all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:26.54,0:23:27.14,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Go on.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.14,0:23:28.02,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Miss Pine,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.84,0:23:30.72,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,may I also call you Nana?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.68,0:23:33.02,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Here is some food.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:33.02,0:23:35.04,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I hope you like it.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.28,0:24:08.02,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Nana.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:11.66,0:24:13.79,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Sister Anna!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:17.21,0:24:20.45,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Thank goodness! Sister Anna, you're alive!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:20.45,0:24:22.16,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,They all said you were dead,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:22.16,0:24:24.58,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,but I knew they were lying.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:26.95,0:24:29.01,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,I've missed you so much.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:31.77,0:24:33.57,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Your Highness, time is short.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:33.57,0:24:35.49,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I must return to the \Nconstruction site immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:35.49,0:24:37.83,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,I will never fail to \Nmeet your expectations.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:38.38,0:24:41.62,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,Anna and Nana... \NI entrust them to your care.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:43.68,0:24:45.43,Main,Karl,0,0,0,,So delicious, Sister Anna!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:44.48,0:24:45.43,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Nana.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:47.07,0:24:49.12,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I heard from Professor Karl
Dialogue: 0,0:24:49.12,0:24:51.27,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,that you've also awakened as a witch.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:54.20,0:24:55.80,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,When did it start?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:56.27,0:24:57.77,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,How did you discover it?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:58.34,0:24:59.66,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Could you tell me about it?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:02.84,0:25:05.42,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,About a week ago,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:05.42,0:25:07.64,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,I saw a little bird with a broken leg,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:07.64,0:25:09.38,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,and I really wanted to help it.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:09.38,0:25:14.30,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,Then, I felt something \Nflow out from my palm,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:14.30,0:25:16.42,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,like a ball of sticky water,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:16.42,0:25:18.10,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,and it enveloped the bird.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:18.10,0:25:19.15,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Oh?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:19.79,0:25:20.84,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,And then?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:21.28,0:25:22.89,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Then...
Dialogue: 0,0:25:22.89,0:25:24.56,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Then the bird was healed!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:26.04,0:25:27.09,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Carter.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:27.09,0:25:28.56,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Oh! Yes, Your Highness?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:29.36,0:25:31.00,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Go into town immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:31.00,0:25:32.72,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Find a hunter and buy some small animals—
Dialogue: 0,0:25:32.72,0:25:35.76,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,injured ones, dying ones, and dead ones.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:35.76,0:25:37.52,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Get a few of each.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:37.52,0:25:38.70,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:50.89,0:25:56.29,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Nana, could you show me \Nthat sticky ball of water again?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:57.08,0:25:59.50,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Don't you want to help them?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:00.40,0:26:01.45,Main,Nana,0,0,0,,Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:28.96,0:26:30.40,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,They're so cute.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:32.71,0:26:33.58,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Look.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:34.79,0:26:36.79,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Damaged parts can be healed.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:37.39,0:26:39.22,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Severed limbs can be perfectly reattached.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:40.46,0:26:42.36,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,But if the limb is lost,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:42.36,0:26:44.59,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,it cannot be regenerated.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:45.22,0:26:46.30,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,And...
Dialogue: 0,0:26:47.42,0:26:49.31,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,death cannot be reversed.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:54.43,0:26:57.22,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,This power is incredible.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:58.21,0:27:00.62,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Saving lives and healing the \Nwounded is a knight's duty.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:01.28,0:27:02.86,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,And yet, it is this little girl
Dialogue: 0,0:27:03.46,0:27:06.94,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,who has shown me what \Nhealing truly looks like.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:06.94,0:27:10.37,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,I really... don't know what to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:11.97,0:27:15.18,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Your Highness, I'm beginning to \Nunderstand your approach to witches.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:15.19,0:27:16.01,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Carter.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:16.01,0:27:17.09,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:17.52,0:27:19.36,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Take her home later.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:19.36,0:27:21.88,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,From now on, find opportunities \Nto bring her here every day,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:21.88,0:27:23.18,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,so she can practice her powers.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:24.00,0:27:26.33,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Why not just keep her here?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:26.33,0:27:28.78,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Her powers are truly astonishing.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:29.61,0:27:30.96,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Her family is nobility.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:31.68,0:27:34.10,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Nana hasn't been exposed as a witch yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:34.10,0:27:35.97,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,If we brought her here now,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:35.97,0:27:39.05,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,it might prematurely start a \Nconflict with the local nobles.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:39.72,0:27:42.91,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,And we're not ready for that yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:42.91,0:27:45.52,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Your Highness, do you truly believe that
Dialogue: 0,0:27:45.52,0:27:49.01,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,we can survive the Months of Demons here,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:49.01,0:27:51.27,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,with just that wall and \Nthe power of witches?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:51.27,0:27:52.11,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:53.28,0:27:56.25,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,But this alone won't be enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:57.79,0:27:59.26,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Because besides the demonic beasts,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:00.32,0:28:02.23,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,we have many more enemies.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:05.97,0:28:09.64,Sign_Basic,CREDITS,0,0,0,,Translator: Henry Lin\NTimer: Henry Lin\NEditor: Zachary Carlysle\N QC: William Haggard
